    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d380-a3">

                <pb facs="0490" n="382" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg382"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate General of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1893-04-12"><hi rendition="#italic">April 12,
                                1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I, Alexander Battiste, deputy consul of the United States at Port au Prince, do
                    hereby certify that the signature above written is the true and genuine
                    signature of Frederick Mevs, made and acknowledged in my presence, and that the
                    said Frederick Mevs is personally known to me.</p>
                <p>In witness thereof, I have hereunto set my hand and affixed the seal of this
                    consulate general this day and year next above written, and of the independence
                    of the United States the one hundred and seventeenth.</p>
                <closer>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">seal.</hi>] <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Alexander Battiste</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Deputy Consul of
                            the United States.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
